9
00:00:33,967 --> 00:00:39,407
Divide that by cosine squared: tangent
squared plus one equals secant squared.

10
00:00:39,857 --> 00:00:45,787
Divide by sine squared instead: one plus
cotangent squared equals cosecant squared.

11
00:00:46,933 --> 00:00:50,069
Simplify sine theta times cotangent theta.

12
00:00:50,519 --> 00:00:56,087
Cotangent is cosine over sine, so the
sines cancel and you get cosine theta.

13
00:00:57,233 --> 00:01:02,843
If sine theta is five thirteenths and
theta is in quadrant two, find cosine

14
00:01:02,843 --> 00:01:03,292
theta.

15
